# SGD Fixed Income Model Portfolio vs Benchmark

*An SGD government and investment-grade bond portfolio positioned against an SGS 2Y–30Y benchmark, with key-rate risk, ex-ante tracking error and six-month scenario attribution, built from MAS benchmark yields as at {{ r.as_of }}.*

## Summary

- **Duration underweight, {{ "%+.2f"|format(A.duration) }} yrs** ({{ "%.2f"|format(P.duration) }} vs {{ "%.2f"|format(B.duration) }}; {{ "%+.1f"|format(A.dv01_sgd/1e3) }} S\$k/bp on S\$500m), held as a hedge for the long-end view rather than a call on direction. The Fed hiked in September, held on 28 October and is guiding higher, and SGS moved about {{ "%.2f"|format(r.oct_move.beta) }}× UST in October; duration P&L is roughly symmetric ({{ "%+.0f"|format(sc.Bull.active_bp.duration) }} bp bull, {{ "%+.0f"|format(sc.Bear.active_bp.duration) }} bp bear), so it is kept small.
- **Curve: DV01-matched 5s30s steepener**, long the 5Y belly against short 20Y–30Y (active KRD 5Y {{ "%+.2f"|format(k.active[1]) }}, 20Y {{ "%+.2f"|format(k.active[4]) }}, 30Y {{ "%+.2f"|format(k.active[5]) }}); entry {{ "%+.0f"|format(r.levels.curve.entry_bp) }} bp, target {{ "%+.0f"|format(r.levels.curve.target_bp) }} bp, stop {{ "%+.0f"|format(r.levels.curve.stop_bp) }} bp. MAS's appreciating S\$NEER slope anchors the front end, while 10s30s at {{ "%+.0f"|format(cv.s10s30) }} bp pays no term premium for long-end risk.
- **SGD IG credit overweight, {{ "%.0f"|format(P.credit_weight*100) }}% of market value** (spread duration {{ "%.2f"|format(P.spread_duration) }} yrs), mostly AAA statutory boards and AA- bank seniors at 4.5–10Y: with a flat curve, spread is the main source of carry. Statutory-board spreads are calibrated to HDB's September 4Y print; hard stop on +{{ r.levels.credit.stop_widening_bp }} bp SGD IG widening.
- **{{ "%+.0f"|format(A.ytm_pct*100) }} bp yield pick-up for {{ "%.0f"|format(r.te.te_bp) }} bp ex-ante tracking error** against a 100 bp budget ({{ "%.0f"|format(r.te.te_6m_bp) }} bp over 6M); over six months the pick-up absorbs about {{ "%.0f"|format(r.breakeven_6m_bp) }} bp of spread widening.
- **Six-month active return:** base **{{ "%+.0f"|format(sc.Base.active_bp.total) }} bp**, bear **{{ "%+.0f"|format(sc.Bear.active_bp.total) }} bp**, bull **{{ "%+.0f"|format(sc.Bull.active_bp.total) }} bp**, credit stress **{{ "%+.0f"|format(sc["Credit stress"].active_bp.total) }} bp**. Credit stress is the main risk, and corporate/REIT lines are cut first.
- **History check (3 years of daily MAS yields): only partial support.** A similar duration underweight lost {{ "%.1f"|format(-HD.mean_bp) }} bp per 6M on average ({{ "%.0f"|format(HD.hit_rate*100) }}% hit rate), so history weakens that call. The steepener earned {{ "%+.1f"|format(HS.mean_bp) }} bp ({{ "%.0f"|format(HS.hit_rate*100) }}% hit rate) from a 5s30s that sits at its 3-year mean (z {{ "%+.2f"|format(HL.s5s30_bp.z) }}). Credit cannot be tested on public data. Conviction is cut to Low (duration) and Medium (curve); position sizes are unchanged.

